  "notes": "Golem spawn in v_tick callocs a living and an an_ent inside the tick, and v_add_door mallocs each door (GPU-contract hazards). DEVLOG says no recording's village collection holds a village yet, so v_tick's golem branch is unexercised by snapshots; test_villagers against out/java/villagers/vil-2 and vil-42 is the evidence. lane/idxclient: the reputation list is name-sorted; every fixed capacity stops the run loudly (village_full) rather than dropping data; the GPU-contract hazards noted before (malloc'd doors, the golem calloc) were already gone (door pool, living pool). idx-villageref-s1 (seed 1, dev): village A is annihilated while its villager still names it; the villager is hit, and the stale Village object takes the aggressor as in Java, so village B's golem stays calm (master's native, whose later villages shifted under the old names, gave B the aggressor and failed at row 305). lane/reloadstate: village-away-s42 leaves the village for 3000 ticks and returns (the village ticks on, 7 doors kept; coverage)."
